# Phadonia project patterns

Use these conventions when editing this codebase.

## Code style

- **Always check `.vscode/settings.json`** before editing and match the project’s formatting.
When in doubt, re-read `.vscode/settings.json` and apply the same style.

## Imports

- Use `import type` for type-only imports.
- Order: React first, then Vercel, then Next, then third-party, then `@/api/...`, then `@/lib/...`, then `@/schema/...`, then `@/json/...`, then `@/` imports.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import { cn } from '@/lib/cn';
import { SilkWrapper } from '@/components/ui/silkWrapper';
```

## Components

- Use functional components only.
- Named exports for reusable components: (e.g `export function Card(...)`).
- Default export only for route components (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`).

## Types

- ~~Prefix type names with `T`: `TCard`, `TLinkButton`, `TProps`, `TRequest`.~~
- Prefer `type` over `interface`; only use `interface` when you need declaration merging or extendable object shapes.

## Styling (Tailwind v4)

- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/cn` for conditional or merged class names.
- Use project design tokens from `app.css`:
  - Surfaces: `body-50` - `body-500`.
  - Accent: `primary-50` - `primary-950`.
  - Text: `text-100` - `text-900`.
- Use custom utility classes when applicable (app.css): `corner-shape-*`, `breakout-wrapper`, `col-full`, `col-sm`, `col-content`, etc.
- For links/buttons, use `@/component/ui/link`.

## Structure

- Components: `src/components/` with feature folders (`Header/`, `Footer/`, `Home/sections/`); primitives in `components/ui/`.
- Shared constants/tokens: `@/lib/util.ts`.
- Schema and types: `@/schema/` with feature folders (`minecraft/`, `wishlist/`).
- Legacy types: `@/types/` with feature folders (`home/`, `minecraft/`), should transition to schema folder.
- SVGR components: `@/svg/...`.

## Other

- Validate external data with Zod; use `validate()` from `@/lib/validate` or `apiFetch()` from `@/lib/apiFetch` when fetching.
